      "text": "First, recall that the formula for the distance between the vertices of a hyperbola in the form $\\frac{y^2}{a^2} - \\frac{x^2}{b^2} = 1$ is $2a$. In this case, we can rewrite the given hyperbola in this form by comparing it to the standard form.\n\nGiven equation: $\\frac{y^2}{27} - \\frac{x^2}{11} = 1$\n\nWe can see that $a^2 = 27$, so $a = \\sqrt{27} = 3\\sqrt{3}$.\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the hyperbola are $(0, \\pm 3\\sqrt{3})$, and the distance between them is $2a = 2 \\cdot 3\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}$.\n\nThe value of the expression $|a-1|$ is not less than $-1$. Determine the value of $a$.  \n\nOptions:\nA) $-1 \\leq a \\leq 1$  \nB) $a \\leq 1$  \nC) $a \\geq 1$  \nD) $a \\leq -1$\n\nTo determine the value of \\( a \\) such that the expression \\( |a-1| \\) is not less than \\(-1\\), we need to analyze the properties of the absolute value function.\n\nThe absolute value function \\( |x| \\) is defined as:\n\\[\n|x| = \n\\begin{cases} \nx & \\text{if } x \\geq 0 \\\\\n-x & \\text{if } x < 0 \n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nIn this case, \\( |a-1| \\) takes the form:\n\\[\n|a-1| = \n\\begin{cases} \na-1 & \\text{if } a-1 \\geq 0 \\\\\n-(a-1) & \\text{if } a-1 < 0 \n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nSimplifying the conditions, we get:\n\\[\n|a-1| = \n\\begin{cases} \na-1 & \\text{if } a \\geq 1 \\\\\n1-a & \\text{if } a < 1 \n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nWe need to ensure that \\( |a-1| \\geq -1 \\). Let's consider both cases:\n\n1. **Case 1: \\( a \\geq 1 \\)**\n   \\[\n   |a-1| = a-1\n   \\]\n   The inequality becomes:\n   \\[\n   a-1 \\geq -1\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( a \\):\n   \\[\n   a-1 + 1 \\geq -1 + 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a \\geq 0\n   \\]\n   Since we already have the condition \\( a \\geq 1 \\), this case is satisfied if \\( a \\geq 1 \\).\n\n2. **Case 2: \\( a < 1 \\)**\n   \\[\n   |a-1| = 1-a\n   \\]\n   The inequality becomes:\n   \\[\n   1-a \\geq -1\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( a \\):\n   \\[\n   1 - a + 1 \\geq -1 + 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2 - a \\geq 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2 \\geq a\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   a \\leq 2\n   \\]\n   Since we already have the condition \\( a < 1 \\), this case is satisfied if \\( a \\leq 1 \\).\n\nCombining both cases, we find that \\( |a-1| \\geq -1 \\) if and only if \\( a \\leq 1 \\).\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( a \\) can be any real number such that \\( a \\leq 1 \\).\n\nThe correct option is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).",
